course: dictionary
lesson: 864
title: A word that sounds posh
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound fancy, and they may not mean what you expect. Estate agents, the people who sell houses, use the word bijou. Read the context: «a bijou cottage» and «a bijou flat» are for sale, so the word must describe a home.
explain: Bijou means small and elegant. But in house adverts it often means very small, the kind of place you would not want to fit a big family in. The agent makes a tiny home sound charming. Always ask: does this word make a small place sound better?
explain: Bijou is French, and in French it means jewel. Long ago it meant a small jewel, a pretty trinket. Today that meaning is rare, so you will mostly meet bijou in a house advert or a story where someone wants to sound grand.
fact: Bijou (adjective) means small and elegant, used about a house or flat.
fact: In UK house adverts, «a bijou flat» often means the flat is very small.
fact: Bijou is a French word, and in French it means jewel.
fact: A bijou (noun, rare) is a small jewel or a pretty trinket.
fact: The plural of the rare noun is bijoux.
exercise: «The flat was a bijou, with room for just one bed.» What does bijou mean here? | Old and falling down | Made of gold | Huge and empty | *Small and neat
exercise: An estate agent writes, «A bijou cottage with a lovely garden.» What is the agent hinting? | The cottage is very old and grand | *The cottage is very small | The cottage is made of jewels | The garden is huge
exercise: The word bijou comes from French. What does a bijou mean as a noun? | A loud noise | *A small jewel or pretty trinket | A kind of cake | A large house in the country
test: Why might an advert say «bijou flat» instead of «tiny flat»? | It means the flat has a swimming pool | *It sounds more charming and pleasant | It is the only correct way to say small | It means the flat is very noisy
test: Which word is a good swap for bijou in «a bijou residence»? | Enormous | *Small and elegant | Ancient | Muddy
exam: Ella reads «a bijou cottage for sale» in a newspaper and asks what it means. What is the best answer? | Huge, with a big garden | Old and crumbling | Shiny and brand new | *Small and neat, often meaning very small
